1
00:00:00,256 --> 00:00:02,205
When maintenance instructions change,

2
00:00:02,261 --> 00:00:04,652
what exactly does an approval still cover?

3
00:00:04,907 --> 00:00:07,987
PhantomDesk is a review desk for a maintenance coordinator.

4
00:00:08,022 --> 00:00:09,685
Its haunted records-office theme

5
00:00:09,686 --> 00:00:11,294
makes one rule visible:

6
00:00:11,435 --> 00:00:14,209
approval belongs to an exact saved revision.

7
00:00:14,464 --> 00:00:16,639
This synthetic request is missing a unit,

8
00:00:16,640 --> 00:00:17,992
so approval is blocked.

9
00:00:18,048 --> 00:00:20,053
I add unit three, save,

10
00:00:20,054 --> 00:00:21,902
and approve the saved instructions.

11
00:00:22,156 --> 00:00:25,258
The intact seal now identifies the approved revision.

12
00:00:25,484 --> 00:00:27,775
Here is the request in the export preview.

13
00:00:27,831 --> 00:00:29,290
I leave the preview open,

14
00:00:29,324 --> 00:00:31,515
change the instructions, and save.

15
00:00:31,799 --> 00:00:32,874
The seal breaks.

16
00:00:32,908 --> 00:00:34,737
The old approval stays in history.

17
00:00:34,843 --> 00:00:37,411
Trying to download the earlier preview is blocked,

18
00:00:37,446 --> 00:00:40,632
because the stored request no longer matches what was approved.

19
00:00:40,944 --> 00:00:46,574
The approval inspector lets me select a preserved approval and compare every field with the current saved record.

20
00:00:46,727 --> 00:00:49,742
Changed and unchanged labels explain the difference.

21
00:00:49,798 --> 00:00:54,109
An unsaved draft is clearly marked and stays separate from the saved comparison.

22
00:00:54,364 --> 00:00:59,393
After reviewing and approving the new revision, I refresh the preview and download a CSV.

23
00:00:59,456 --> 00:01:02,399
Its instructions, revision, and approval time

24
00:01:02,400 --> 00:01:03,766
match the saved approval.

25
00:01:03,936 --> 00:01:07,059
A later matching request creates another review condition.

26
00:01:07,264 --> 00:01:08,970
Both requests stay in the ledger,

27
00:01:08,971 --> 00:01:11,061
and the earlier approval expires.

28
00:01:11,214 --> 00:01:14,685
Resolving one pair does not automatically resolve a third request.

29
00:01:14,969 --> 00:01:17,613
The app uses JavaScript and the browser's database,

30
00:01:17,614 --> 00:01:19,649
with no runtime AI service.

31
00:01:19,876 --> 00:01:22,069
Codex authored the original prototype.

32
00:01:22,156 --> 00:01:25,312
Kiro CLI implemented the approval comparison helper,

33
00:01:25,313 --> 00:01:27,488
historical selector, styles,

34
00:01:27,489 --> 00:01:29,865
and additional tests from the project brief.

35
00:01:29,964 --> 00:01:33,044
Independent Codex review corrected comparison details,

36
00:01:33,164 --> 00:01:35,762
selection stability, and draft behavior.

37
00:01:35,826 --> 00:01:37,989
Automated checks and browser verification

38
00:01:38,087 --> 00:01:39,937
cover the demonstrated workflow.

39
00:01:40,135 --> 00:01:42,405
This prototype stores records on this device.

40
00:01:42,439 --> 00:01:45,114
Reviewer labels are not authenticated identities.

41
00:01:45,341 --> 00:01:47,239
Try changing an approved request.

42
00:01:47,457 --> 00:01:49,150
The old approval stays visible.

43
00:01:49,249 --> 00:01:52,002
The changed instructions have to earn a new seal.
